Detonator patch for OpenSSF package-analysis (sandboxes/dynamicanalysis/analyze-node.js).

Problem: install() calls process.exit(1) when `npm install` returns non-zero, which
aborts the analysis before the `import` phase. rundynamic.go skips subsequent phases
on failure, so `import` (require(pkg.name), which fires require-time payloads) never
runs for any package whose install exits non-zero (dep-resolution failures, audit/peer
warnings). See docs/eval/2026-07-23-phase2-import-coverage-finding.md.

Fix: don't exit on install failure — log and continue so the import phase still runs.

Apply on the burner, then rebuild + load the sandbox image:
  cd /opt/package-analysis
  patch -p1 < analyze-node-import-on-install-fail.patch
  make build/sandbox/dynamic_analysis RELEASE_TAG=latest
  docker save gcr.io/ossf-malware-analysis/dynamic-analysis:latest -o /tmp/da.tar
  docker run --rm --privileged -v /var/lib/containers:/var/lib/containers -v /tmp/da.tar:/da.tar \
    --entrypoint podman gcr.io/ossf-malware-analysis/analysis:latest load -i /da.tar
  # retag the loaded image to gcr.io/ossf-malware-analysis/dynamic-analysis:latest

--- a/sandboxes/dynamicanalysis/analyze-node.js
+++ b/sandboxes/dynamicanalysis/analyze-node.js
@@ -27,8 +27,11 @@
     // Always exit on failure.
     // Install failing is either an interesting issue, or an opportunity to
     // improve the analysis.
-    console.log('Install failed.');
-    process.exit(1);
+    // Detonator patch: do NOT abort on non-zero npm install. npm exits non-zero
+    // for benign reasons (audit/peer warnings) and for dep-resolution failures, but
+    // the target package is usually still unpacked into node_modules — so continue
+    // so the import phase runs require(pkg.name) and fires any require-time payload.
+    console.log('Install failed (continuing to import phase).');
   }
 }
